                        "language": "english",
                        "review": "32 levels, 51 (\"52\") secrets to find, 1 boss fight.\n\nI played through the entire game without using any upgrades due to one achievement asking me to do so which resulted in an experience that was probably a lot less fun than intended, but I think the game would be very enjoyable to play through if you did it with the available upgrades. The double jump and shockwave are exceptionally helpful, but I only got to experience them for a fraction of the game. The cube level was fantastic, by far my favorite and the boss fight was... probably the worst, but again: that might be due to the fact that I had 0 upgrades for it.\n\nIf you're the type to enjoy games like A Game About Digging a Hole or Leaf it Alone, you'd probably get a lot of satisfaction out of completely cleaning the dirt out of every level in this game. That's [b]NOT[/b] the goal of the game at all, but it does lead to finding minerals that let you upgrade your character more.\n\nYou get a really cool grappling hook upgrade for finding all 51 secrets which would make replaying the game interesting to say the least as [i]I assume[/i] it wouldn't be limited in scenarios where building or placing forcefields is. You could probably skip a LOT of each level using it if you went back to them for a replay with it.",
